Atari 800 / 800XL / 65XE / 130XE for the Sipeed Tang Nano 20K
=============================================================
LICENSING OVERVIEW

This repository is NOT under a single licence. It combines an upstream Atari
8-bit core, several third-party FPGA and firmware components, and original work
written for this Tang Nano 20K port. Each part keeps the licence its author gave
it. This file is the map; the full texts are in LICENSES/.

Every source file's own header notice is authoritative for that file. Do not
remove or alter those headers.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EFFECTIVE TERMS OF THE COMBINED WORK — NON-COMMERCIAL
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Atari machine implementation this project is built on (Mark Watson's
atari800core, as distributed in Atari800_MiSTer) is offered for NON-COMMERCIAL
USE ONLY, in source and binary form and for derived works.

Therefore the project as a whole — this repository, and any bitstream built
from it, including the .fs files published on the Releases page — may be used
and redistributed for NON-COMMERCIAL PURPOSES ONLY.

Selling this core, selling boards preloaded with it, or otherwise using it
commercially requires explicit permission from Mark Watson (scrameta@gmail.com),
and additionally from the other copyright holders listed below whose licences do
not already permit it.

Note that this is stricter than the licences of several individual components:
a permissively licensed file (Apache-2.0, MIT, ISC, BSD) may of course still be
taken from this tree and used commercially under its own terms, on its own.


